ldm (3.0.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Fixed: ldm never actually started at boot on a real PXE-booted LTSP
    client. The package installed the ldm binary and its themes but never
    registered it as THE display manager: no systemd service unit, no
    /etc/X11/default-display-manager entry, so systemd's graphical.target
    had nothing to launch and boot fell through to a plain text getty
    login instead. Added debian/ldm.service (with the standard
    "Alias=display-manager.service" that dh_installsystemd turns into the
    /etc/systemd/system/display-manager.service symlink real display
    managers rely on) and had ldm.postinst/.prerm set/clear
    /etc/X11/default-display-manager, which ltsp6's own
    init-ltsp.d/50-default-display-manager hook already expects to exist.
    Found via a real end-to-end PXE boot test (DHCP -> TFTP -> NBD root ->
    switch_root), not just direct/manual ldm invocation.

 -- Marc-André Beckmann-Butz <ma@butz.online>  Wed, 02 Sep 2026 09:20:00 +0200

ldm (3.0.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Version bumped from the upstream 2.18.06 baseline to 3.0.0: porting
    gtkgreet from GTK2 to GTK3 is a breaking change for anyone still
    building the old tree (GTK2 is gone from Debian's archive, so 2.18.06
    no longer builds at all), on top of the new xfreerdp backend and the
    security/correctness fixes below - substantial enough to warrant a
    major version bump rather than a patch-level one.
  * Fork of the last upstream ldm release (2:2.18.06, last packaged for
    Debian Buster) by Marc-André Beckmann-Butz, updated to build and run
    on current Debian releases:
    - Ported gtkgreet from GTK2 to GTK3 (GTK2 was removed from Debian's
      archive, so upstream ldm no longer builds at all).
    - Added an xfreerdp backend plugin: auto-detects xfreerdp3/xfreerdp2,
      supports an optional default RDP domain, and passes credentials to
      xfreerdp via stdin instead of the command line (argv is readable by
      any local user via /proc/<pid>/cmdline or ps).
    - Fixed an argv-based process spawning issue shared by the ssh and
      xfreerdp plugins: commands were built as strings and word-split by
      glib, which both mis-handled usernames/passwords containing spaces
      or quotes, and, in the ssh plugin, allowed unauthenticated argument
      injection (e.g. a crafted username at the login prompt could smuggle
      an ssh ProxyCommand and run arbitrary code as root).
    - Fixed a heap buffer overflow in the LTSP-Cluster load-balancer
      client (get_ltsp_cfg()), a path-traversal issue in the host-info
      reader (ldminfo.c), NULL-pointer-dereference crashes in the plugin
      dispatch and ssh guest-login code paths, and an undefined-behaviour
      va_list misuse between log_entry()/die().
    - Enabled standard hardening compiler/linker flags
      (_FORTIFY_SOURCE, stack-protector, RELRO, PIE for the executables).
    - Fixed a window-placement bug in wwm (forked from evilwm) where
      newly mapped windows without WM_NORMAL_HINTS' USPosition set had
      their already-placed position discarded in favour of a synthesized
      centred placement.

 -- Marc-André Beckmann-Butz <ma@butz.online>  Mon, 31 Aug 2026 22:30:00 +0200
